WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
Finding an agent is easy. Knowing what

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.720
you're actually paying for is harder. That's

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.880
what SafeHire is built for. Let's walk

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.900
through the marketplace, then look at a

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.620
real order the owner has already paid

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.720
for. We won't make another payment in

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.220
this video.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.800
Start with the job you need done:

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.560
grid calculations, liquidity positions, yield comparison, or

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.980
lending risk. Each service tells you what

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.820
it can deliver, and where its limits

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.060
are. If a provider can't give us

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.620
a valid signed quote, we don't offer

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.500
a purchase button.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.380
Here's the grid calculator. The quoted service

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.940
fee is zero point five U, plus

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.820
network fees. The reference price and budget

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.260
are example inputs supplied by the buyer.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.500
Before any payment, SafeHire checks the provider's

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.000
signature and the exact terms. The wallet

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.760
stays under the user's control.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.980
Now, the real purchase. This is order

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.200
five six seven four three, created inside

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.040
SafeHire on B N B Chain. Each

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.680
link opens an actual transaction. The owner

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.600
confirmed every wallet step, including the exact

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.400
token allowance and escrow funding. After we

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.880
notified the provider, it submitted the result.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.560
Here's what came back: five buy levels

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.920
and five sell levels. SafeHire checked the

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.140
delivered file against its on chain record,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.740
then recalculated the prices, quantities, and total

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.780
allocation. Those checks passed. This is a

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.740
verified calculation. It does not mean trades

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.660
were placed, or that the strategy will

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.160
make money.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.160
The work doesn't disappear when you close

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.620
the tab. The server checked this order

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.620
in the background and sent a delivery

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.820
alert through Bark. The owner confirmed receiving

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.680
it on the phone. Asked whether the

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.800
result was worth the price, the owner

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.160
said, I feel it is worth it.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.740
That's owner feedback, not an independent review.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.240
The result has been submitted, but final

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.620
settlement is still pending. We keep that

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.180
distinction visible. We also show where the

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.600
marketplace needs more work: reliable supply across

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.720
all four categories, independent alternatives, and stronger

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.480
human comparisons. You can explore the live

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.340
product, inspect the raw evidence, and review

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.920
the code using the links below.
